<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahoba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahoba is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>, in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and the headquarters of the district of the same name. It was one of the capitals of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandela-dynasty">Chandela dynasty</a>, whose kings built large artificial lakes there such as the Madan Sagar. Mahoba is celebrated in the Alha-Khand ballads of the warriors Alha and Udal, who fought for the Chandela king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paramardi">Paramardi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahoba.jpg" alt="Mahoba" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anshulmahoba · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MAHOBA,_U.P._-_allha.preview.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
